<mxCell id="l15c40" value="build([1, 2, 3])   # Python list → linked list&lt;br&gt;to_list(head)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;  # linked list → Python list&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;for case in ([], [1], [1, 2], [1, 2, 3]):&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;assert to_list(reverse_iter(build(case))) == case[::-1]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=11;fillColor=#272822;fontColor=#f8f8f2;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="450" width="520" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="l15c41" value="Comparing with == on plain lists makes failures readable.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In real code, collections.deque (a doubly linked list of blocks) gives O(1) at both ends." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="580" y="450" width="280" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
